main":false,"recentAcquisition":false,"referenceNumber":"","relatedObjects":[],"state":"","support":[],"technique":["Cotton plain-weave ground embroidered with indigo-dyed silk in satin and couching stitches"],"title":"Suzanni (embroidered wall hanging)","type":["Textiles"],"url":"https:\/\/risdmuseum.org\/art-design\/collection\/suzanni-embroidered-wall-hanging-200653"},{"id":"1539081","collection":"","credit":"Helen M. Danforth Acquisition Fund","culture":"","dating":"","datingYearFrom":"1825","datingYearTo":"1855","description":"\u003Cp\u003EEntrance to a Chalet in the Bernese Oberland (nt\u00e9rieur d\u0027un Chalet d\u0027Oberland Bernois)\u003C\/p\u003E\n","dimensions":"25.9 x 37.6 cm (10 3\/16 x 14 13\/16 inches) Dimensions verified 12\/22\/2004","edition":"","inscription":"Stamped LL in red:VENTE\/ COROT\nSeals: In the center, center of the strainer is a red wax seal.Written upside down on this label are the words \u0022VENTE \/COROT\u0022. written upside down \u0022VENTE \/ COROT\u0022\nMarks: In the upper center of the verso frame, written in blue (possibly pencil) are an encircled \u002243\u0022 to the right of which there are written the letters \u0022L\u0022 (possibly a \u0022z\u0022) followed by a \u0022P\u0022.To the right of the blue writing, in pencil is written the RISD accession number, \u002254.175\u0022.In the upper right corner of the verso frame, in pencil is written \u0022CASE 59822\/15\u0022.In the left center of the verso frame on a piece of masking tape in ink, is written \u0022COROT (separating dot) BO...[obscured by a metal hanging device] 4\u0022. In the upper right corner of the strainer, written in red pencil are three illegible numbers, then the numbers \u0022961[illegible number]5\u0022.Beneath these numbers in bluish pencil are more illegible numbers.In the upper center of the canvas in black ink is an oval stamp with the writing \u0022DL TRIMONT \/ [illegible] \/ [illegible] \/[illegible]\u0022. On the backing board in the upper right corner, written in pencil is the number \u0022737\u0022.In the Upper right quadrant of the backing board in red marker is the RISD accession number \u002254.175\u0022.\nLabel: In the upper left quadrant of the verso strainer is an old label with a typed \u0022No.\u0022 followed by (in ink) \u002225105 \/ Corot \/ INTERIEUR D\u0027UN CHALET DE \/ L\u0027OBERLAND BERNOIS p.r.v. \/ Vente Corot no 124 \/ No 731 du r[?]ohau[illegible letter, n?]\u0022.In the upper right corner of the strainer is a rectangular label with a blue beveled border.In the center of the label written in pencil is the number \u00224038\u0022.In the lower right corner of the strainer is the remnants of a removed label.To the left of the remnant is an old rectangular label with a typewritten \u0022No.\u0022 followed by (in blue ink) \u002219978\u0022 \/ Corot \/ Landschaft\u0022.On the backing board in the upper Left corner is a new RISD museum label with a red border.In the upper center of the backing board is a red \u0022Do Not Touch\u0022 label. In the upper right corner is an Arts COuncil of Great Britian label (probably a loan label).In the lower right quadrant is a label for the exhibition \u0022The Spirit of Barbizon #3\u0022.In the lower right corner is a label for a Corot exhibition that traveled to the RMN, NGC and MMA.In the lower center of the backing board is a label for the Metropolitan Museum of Art from 1997 for an exhibit on Corot.IN the Left center is a label for the National museum in Paris \u0022Reunion de musees nationaux Paris\u0022 from 1996.","makers":[{"name":"Jean-Baptiste-Camille Corot","risdAffiliation":null,"years":"1796-1875","nationality":["French"],"nationalityModifiers":null,"role":null,"attribution_type":null}],"medium":["Oil on canvas"],"mediumTechnique":"oil paint","objectNumber":"54.175","onView":false,"place":"Place Made: Switzerland","primaryMaker":"Jean-Baptiste-Camille Corot","publicDomain":false,"recentAcquisition":false,"referenceNumber":"","relatedObjects":[],"state":"","support":["canvas"],"technique":["Oil on canvas"],"title":"Entrance to a Chalet in the Bernese Oberland (nt\u00e9rieur d\u0026#039;un Chalet d\u0026#039;Oberland Bernois)","type":["Paintings"],"url":"https:\/\/risdmuseum.org\/art-design\/collection\/entrance-chalet-bernese-oberland-nterieur-dun-chalet-doberland-bernois-54175"}]